cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this pattern, please cite it as below."
title: "The Ambassador Agent pattern: one accountable agent per external-system boundary"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zohdy
    given-names: Bassem
version: 0.2.2
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24210615
date-released: 2026-11-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/bassemZohdy/ambassador-agent"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A proposed design pattern for agentic integration platforms. Every
  external-system boundary gets exactly one autonomous agent that answers
  for everything that crosses it. The repository holds the specification,
  numbered conformance rules, worked examples and a small reference
  implementation. It is a proposal open for critique and has no documented
  use in production yet.
keywords:
  - design pattern
  - ai agents
  - software architecture
  - system integration
  - idempotency
